# Compiled class file
*.class

# Log file
*.log

# BlueJ files
*.ctxt

# Mobile Tools for Java (J2ME)
.mtj.tmp/

# Package Files #
*.jar
*.war
*.nar
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar
# ...except the Gradle wrapper jar, which MUST be committed (it's the bootstrap jar `./gradlew`
# invokes to download the real Gradle distribution -- without it, `./gradlew` fails with
# "Unable to access jarfile .../gradle-wrapper.jar"). This blanket *.jar rule silently excluded it
# from every commit (local and the GitLab "Platform snapshot" re-push alike, since that re-push
# re-applies this same .gitignore in a fresh `git init`), which broke the trusted-supply-chain
# pipeline's build-image task for every Gradle-based service (app/, app/camel-ai-router/).
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# virtual machine crash logs, see http://www.java.com/en/download/help/error_hotspot.xml
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

.idea/
.gradle/
build/
.env